  "The Paw Passport · a field guide · PDF",
  "Crossing borders with a dog, without the part where you cry at a checkpoint.",
  "Written from 13 countries and one transatlantic flight, by someone whose dog weighs 35 kilos and has opinions. The law is the free part. What happened at the border at 11pm with a Samoyed in the back is the part you pay for.",
  "On the house · read it first",
  "Four ways to get turned back at a border with your dog.",
  "The four mistakes, in full, because they are the most searched and the most useful. Three of the four are about order, not paperwork.",
  "Free",
  "Chip first, then the rabies shot. The other way round does not count.",
  "Free",
  "21 days, counted from the end of the protocol, not from booking the ferry.",
  "Free",
  "The booster has to land inside the old one. Miss it by a day and the clock restarts.",
  "Free",
  "Puppies: 12 weeks at the shot, then 21 days. Roughly 15 weeks before a first border.",
  "In the guide",
  "✓",
